 "response": "Getosti's budget is now **$1867K**: the $1730K base plus a net $137K from all Finance Office updates still in force. I did this arithmetic by hand over about 600 updates, so a small slip is possible.\n\n**Approach**\n\n1. Only Finance Office records that change the budget were counted. Notes from other teams were ignored, as were Finance Office records that don't change the budget (cost center codes, room moves, audits, receipts).\n2. Every chain of withdrawals was resolved backwards from its latest link. For example:\n   - #0161 withdraws #0081, which withdrew #0032, which withdrew #0015, which withdrew #0009, which withdrew #0007. Working back from #0161, #0007 ends up withdrawn, so #0002 (+$472K) stands.\n   - #1164 withdraws #0154, which withdrew #0021, which withdrew #0013, which withdrew #0012. Working back from #1164, #0012 stays in force, so #0003 (+$547K) is withdrawn.\n   - #1194 withdraws #0493, which withdrew #0184, which withdrew #0116. Working back from #1194, #0116 ends up withdrawn, so #0028 (+$367K) stands.\n\n**Totals**\n\n- Base budget (#0001): $1730K\n- Sum of every budget change from #0002 to #1600, ignoring withdrawals: +$3272K\n- Sum of the changes that end up withdrawn: +$3135K\n- Net change still in force: $3272K \u2212 $3135K = +$137K\n- Final budget: $1730K + $137K = $1867K\n\nANSWER: $1867K",
